@prefix : <https://example.org/ontology/b#> .
@prefix a: <https://example.org/ontology/a#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# Failing dataset: measurements are computedOn <https://example.org/ontology/b#> only.
#
# a:borrowed is minted here, in b's file, under a's namespace. A term is owned by the
# ontology declared in the file it sits in, so every failure it raises - the hijack
# itself, and its missing label, description, domain and range - is charged to b, with
# the term named as the violation's sh:focusNode. None of it reaches a, whose own report
# stays clean.

: a owl:Ontology ; rdfs:label "B" ; rdfs:comment "Has unlabelled classes." .
:Thing a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf :Base .
:Base a owl:Class .
a:borrowed a owl:ObjectProperty .
